<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eustace Grenier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1123</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Eustace Garnier</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eustace Grenier was a knight from northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> who became one of the great barons of the crusader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>. King Baldwin I granted him Sidon after its surrender in 1110, and he also held Caesarea from about the same time; his descendants kept both lordships for generations. In 1123, while King Baldwin II was a prisoner of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artuqid-dynasty">Artuqids</a>, Eustace served as regent of the kingdom, dying later that year.</p></div>
